"All settings — configuration editor\nlanguage = auto\n  accepts: auto or a language tag such as en, fr or es-419; source: default; The conversation language: auto answers in the question's language; a tag such as fr or es-419 answers in that one. Code and documentation stay in English.\n  Editable in user preferences.\ntone = normal\n  accepts: one of brief, normal, detailed; source: default; How much an answer explains: brief, normal, or detailed (shown as Very detailed). Prose only; code and documents are unchanged.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nsearch.k = 10\n  accepts: a whole number from 1 to 50; source: default; The most passages a search returns when --k (the MCP k) is not given.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nsearch.evidence_bytes = 12000\n  accepts: a whole number from 1 to 24000; source: default; A search's evidence budget, in UTF-8 bytes, when --evidence-bytes is not given.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nsearch.deadline_ms = 30000\n  accepts: a whole number from 1 to 30000; source: default; A search's deadline in milliseconds when --deadline-ms is not given.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nsearch.routes.dense = true\n  accepts: true or false; source: default; Whether the dense (embedding) route runs, in searches and asks.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nsearch.routes.lexical = true\n  accepts: true or false; source: default; Whether the lexical route runs, in searches and asks.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nsearch.routes.identifier = true\n  accepts: true or false; source: default; Whether the exact-identifier route runs, in searches and asks.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nsearch.routes.structured = true\n  accepts: true or false; source: default; Whether the structured route may run for global questions, in searches and asks.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nsearch.routes.limit = 100\n  accepts: a whole number from 1 to 120; source: default; The maximum dense, lexical and intent candidates; identifier retrieval also uses its identifier limit.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nsearch.routes.identifier_limit = 20\n  accepts: a whole number from 1 to 120; source: default; The maximum identifier candidates, additionally bounded by search.routes.limit.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nsearch.identifier.noise_guard = false\n  accepts: true or false; source: default; Whether the identifier route drops identifiers too common to rank, and fusion takes no hits from an unavailable route, in searches and asks.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nsearch.rrf_k = 60\n  accepts: a whole number from 1 to 1000; source: default; The reciprocal rank fusion constant K.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nsearch.weights.dense = 1\n  accepts: a number from 0 to 100; source: default; The dense route's weight in fusion.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nsearch.weights.lexical = 1\n  accepts: a number from 0 to 100; source: default; The lexical route's weight in fusion.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nsearch.weights.identifier = 1\n  accepts: a number from 0 to 100; source: default; The exact-identifier route's weight in fusion.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nsearch.weights.structured = 1\n  accepts: a number from 0 to 100; source: default; The structured route's weight in fusion.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nsearch.rerank.enabled = true\n  accepts: true or false; source: default; Whether the reranker reorders the fused candidates.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nsearch.fusion_pool = 120\n  accepts: a whole number from 1 to 120; source: default; The maximum candidates retained by fusion; rerank depth cannot exceed this value.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nsearch.rerank.depth = 30\n  accepts: a whole number from 1 to 120; source: default; How many fused candidates the reranker reads.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nsearch.rerank.blend = off\n  accepts: a number from 0 to 1, or \"off\"; source: default; The fused position's weight in a fusion with the rerank order; off keeps the rerank order.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nsearch.rerank.demotion_cap = off\n  accepts: a whole number from 0 to 120, or \"off\"; source: default; The most positions reranking may drop a fused top-10 candidate; off sets no cap.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nsearch.rerank.context = chunk\n  accepts: one of chunk, bounded_section; source: default; What the reranker reads: the indexed chunk, or its whole section when that fits search.rerank.context_max_bytes.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nsearch.rerank.context_max_bytes = 1500\n  accepts: a whole number from 1 to 1500; source: default; The most bytes of section context the reranker reads under bounded_section.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nsearch.section_prior.weight = off\n  accepts: a number from 0 to 1, or \"off\"; source: default; How much of their fusion score the sections of search.section_prior.classes lose, unless the question names them; off leaves the order as it is.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nsearch.section_prior.classes = changelog,release_notes,conversion\n  accepts: some of changelog, release_notes, conversion, each at most once; source: default; The section classes search.section_prior.weight applies to.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nsearch.stage_window_ms = off\n  accepts: a whole number from 1 to 30000, or \"off\"; source: default; A fixed route window in milliseconds, for experiments; off derives it from the deadline.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nsearch.intent.expansion = off\n  accepts: one of off, hyde; source: default; Whether a search adds a guarded hypothetical passage, written by the collection's answerer, as extra retrieval routes: off, or hyde.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nsearch.intent.min_top_rerank = off\n  accepts: a number from -100 to 100, or \"off\"; source: default; Under hyde, expand only when the best rerank score is below this one; off expands every search.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nsearch.intent.deadline_ms = 4000\n  accepts: a whole number from 1 to 5000; source: default; The most milliseconds the intent expansion may take, within the search deadline.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nsearch.intent.weight = 1\n  accepts: a number from 0 to 100; source: default; Each intent route's weight in fusion.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nsearch.intent.rerank_additions = 10\n  accepts: a whole number from 0 to 120; source: default; The most candidates the intent routes may add beyond rerank depth; the combined candidates can exceed search.fusion_pool.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nsearch.source_prior.weight = 0.6\n  accepts: a number from 0 to 1, or \"off\"; source: default; How much of their fusion score documents of search.source_prior.classes lose, so official pages rank first; off leaves the order as it is.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nsearch.source_prior.classes = official_code,community,third_party,internal_code\n  accepts: some of official_docs, official_kb, official_code, community, third_party, internal_code, each at most once; source: default; The source classes search.source_prior.weight applies to.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nevidence.expansion = parent_chain\n  accepts: one of full_section, relevant_blocks, parent_chain; source: default; How evidence grows around a match: its full section first, or its matched blocks first, or complete parent-chain ranges first.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nevidence.parent_chain_order = minimum_complete_first\n  accepts: one of off, minimum_complete_first, largest_fitting_parent; source: default; Admission order for parent_chain expansion only; minimum_complete_first reserves the smallest complete unit first.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nevidence.counter = utf8\n  accepts: one of utf8, utf8_answer_bound; source: default; What the evidence budget counts: every passage byte, or only the bytes the answerer reads.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nask.model = ask-gemma4-e4b-nonthinking\n  accepts: a router entry: 1 to 64 ASCII letters, digits, '.', '_' and '-', never '.' or '..' alone; source: default; The answerer's router entry when --model (the MCP model) is not given.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nask.prompt = v2\n  accepts: one of v1, v2, procedure_first; source: default; The answer prompt's version.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nask.k = 5\n  accepts: a whole number from 1 to 50; source: default; The most passages an answer reads when --k is not given.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nask.evidence_bytes = 6000\n  accepts: a whole number from 1 to 24000; source: default; An answer's evidence budget, in UTF-8 bytes, when --evidence-bytes is not given.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nask.search_deadline_ms = 30000\n  accepts: a whole number from 1 to 30000; source: default; An answer's search deadline in milliseconds when --search-deadline-ms is not given.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nask.output_tokens = off\n  accepts: a whole number from 1 to 2048, or \"off\"; source: default; The most tokens each answerer reply generates when --output-tokens is not given; off takes the answerer card's output limit, or 1024 when it declares none.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nask.min_rerank_score = off\n  accepts: a number from -100 to 100, or \"off\"; source: default; The least top reranker score an answer is given passages from; off answers whatever the score. Search results are never filtered by it.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nmodels.compute = gpu\n  accepts: one of off, gpu; source: default; Where models run: gpu, the machine's GPU backend (CUDA or Metal), or off for code only: search keeps its keyword, exact-name and structured routes without reranking, and ask refuses. cpu comes after M1.\n  Editable in user preferences.\ngraph.engine = none\n  accepts: one of none, ladybug; source: default; The local knowledge graph: none makes no graph calls; ladybug selects the embedded LadybugDB adapter in a build with the engine feature. No server or download.\n  Editable in user preferences.\ngraphdb.buffer_pool_size = 268435456\n  accepts: a whole number from 16777216 to 1073741824; source: default; Graph buffer pool bytes; zero/automatic sizing is not supported.\n  Editable in user preferences.\ngraphdb.max_db_size = 17179869184\n  accepts: a whole number from 16777216 to 1099511627776, a power of two; source: default; Maximum graph database address space in bytes, a power of two; not a disk quota.\n  Editable in user preferences.\ngraphdb.max_num_threads = 2\n  accepts: a whole number from 1 to 64; source: default; Maximum graph query threads; unrelated to Cargo parallelism.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nchunking.profile = mapped-structural-chunks/3\n  accepts: one of mapped-structural-chunks/2, mapped-structural-chunks/3; source: default; Default for new collections; published profiles persist unless --chunk-profile overrides.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nupdates = propose\n  accepts: one of off, propose, auto; source: default; Updates narrow off < propose < auto; auto is user-only; runtime and MCP never auto-apply.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nmodel_profile = balanced\n  accepts: one of fast, balanced, deep; source: default; Qualified models per role; a stored profile is not qualification or execution permission.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nreasoning_effort = default\n  accepts: one of default; source: default; Model default; unsupported requested levels diagnose rather than being ignored.\n  Editable in user preferences.\ninference_writers = 1\n  accepts: a whole number from 1 to 1; source: default; Maximum concurrent inference requests; default one.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nworkspace_writers = 1\n  accepts: a whole number from 1 to 1; source: default; Maximum concurrent workspace writers; default one.\n  Editable in user preferences.\ndelegation_depth = 2\n  accepts: a whole number from 0 to 2; source: default; Maximum delegation depth; default two.\n  Editable in user preferences.\ntool_calls = 40\n  accepts: a whole number from 0 to 40; source: default; Maximum tool calls per ask run; default forty.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nrepair_attempts = 2\n  accepts: a whole number from 0 to 2; source: default; Maximum contract repair attempts; default two.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nrouting_candidates = 3\n  accepts: a whole number from 1 to 3; source: default; Maximum routing candidates; default three.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nmcp_call_timeout = 30000\n  accepts: a whole number from 1 to 30000; source: default; MCP call timeout in milliseconds within the server profile.\n  Editable in user preferences.\ncross_project_memory = false\n  accepts: true or false; source: default; Cross-project memory is off until qualified.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nmcp_apps = false\n  accepts: true or false; source: default; MCP Apps are off until activated.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nextensions = false\n  accepts: true or false; source: default; Extensions are off until activated.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nschedules = false\n  accepts: true or false; source: default; Schedules are off until activated.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nraw_prompt_logging = false\n  accepts: true or false; source: default; Raw prompt logging is off in the initial profile.\n  Locked: no file or flag may edit; inspect with `maestro config explain`.\nraw_reasoning_logging = false\n  accepts: true or false; source: default; Raw reasoning logging is off in the initial profile.\n  Locked: no file or flag may edit; inspect with `maestro config explain`.\nprovider_fallback = none\n  accepts: one of none; source: default; Provider fallback is disabled in the initial profile.\n  Locked: no file or flag may edit; inspect with `maestro config explain`.\nevidence_validation = true\n  accepts: true or false; source: default; Evidence validation is on in the initial profile.\n  Locked: no file or flag may edit; inspect with `maestro config explain`.\nresult_validation = true\n  accepts: true or false; source: default; Result validation is on in the initial profile.\n  Locked: no file or flag may edit; inspect with `maestro config explain`.\ndiscovered_executable_hooks = false\n  accepts: true or false; source: default; Discovered executable hooks are off in the initial profile.\n  Locked: no file or flag may edit; inspect with `maestro config explain`.\nworkflow.budgets.tokens = 2147483647\n  accepts: a whole number from 0 to 2147483647; source: default; Maximum input and output tokens per workflow, including child runs; no cap by default, as in Pi.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nworkflow.budgets.wall_ms = 1800000\n  accepts: a whole number from 1 to 2147483647; source: default; Maximum elapsed milliseconds per workflow, including waits; thirty minutes by default, as in Pi.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nworkflow.budgets.tool_calls = 2147483647\n  accepts: a whole number from 0 to 2147483647; source: default; Maximum total tool calls per workflow, including child runs; no cap by default, as in Pi.\n  Editable in user preferences.\nTrust is authority, not a preference: use `maestro trust add`, `list` or `remove`.\nSetting KEY=VALUE [Enter reviews; back/cancel]: \n"
